      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While increased water intake is the cornerstone of stone management, attempting to self-treat with high-dose supplements is risky. High doses of Vitamin C can potentially increase oxalate levels in the urine, which is the direct component of your stones, rather than clearing them. It is safest to adhere to your doctor's primary recommendation and discuss specific dietary or supplement tools with them before making drastic changes.",
